1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,894
In the year 2451 the surface of the Earth is bright and tired. Rivers are measured. Cities are fenced. Under all of it, a country no map has ever held is still lighting its lamps.

2
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:13,617
Many nations share one office, the Telluric Compact. Dr. Imani Okonkwo hears a chord return every one hundred and eight seconds. Stone does not keep time like that. Someone is keeping it.

3
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:12,766
They dig toward the chord. The drill grows warm before it breaks through. On the other side is a stair, dry and swept, lit by lamps that leave no smoke.

4
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:15,745
Asha, keeper of the upper lamps, is on the stair with a broom. She looks at the drill and then at the people. She is not afraid. A guest, she was taught, arrives when the guest arrives.

5
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:12,340
Asha says, You have found the door. The door was never locked. It was only quiet. That night Imani writes the word home, deletes it, and writes it again.

6
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:13,191
Water comes in clay cups. No one is searched. No one is told to kneel. Pema the healer binds a split knuckle and will not take the coin offered for it.

7
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:10,638
By morning the Compact has its own words. Asset. Aperture. Strategic reserve. They draw a circle around the mountain and call the circle a site.

8
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:14,043
Commander Vale arrives with the flags of the joined nations. He is polite. He posts guards, he says, until the law arrives. Asha sets a lamp in the window of the guard tent.

9
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:14,043
They do not build a city yet. They hammer pegs into the dust and string a white line. Below that line, the lamps of Shambhala burn at the hour they have always burned.

10
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:14,468
The decade ends over two suppers. Above, rations. Below, a long table, and an empty chair for the guest who has not decided to sit. The chair will wait. It will not be removed.
